# Tor as a plain HTTP CONNECT proxy, for one caller: PrivatBank's document
# service. See PrivatbankProxyService for why that one path needs a route of
# its own, and why nothing else is on it.

# No SOCKS listener. Nothing here speaks SOCKS — the API's agent is
# `https-proxy-agent`, which speaks HTTP CONNECT — and a port nobody uses is a
# port nobody has to reason about.
SocksPort 0

# The tunnel, reachable only from the compose network this container is on: no
# host port is published for it, exactly as none is for the database. It has no
# authentication of its own and needs none for the same reason Mongo and Redis
# do not have one inside the network — but it is an open proxy to anything that
# can reach it, so that segment is the whole of its protection.
#
# `IsolateSOCKSAuth` is what makes the pool work, and it applies to the
# credentials presented to this tunnel too. Each distinct proxy username gets a
# circuit of its own, and the same username keeps the one it has. So the
# entries in PRIVATBANK_PROXY_URLS differ only in their username: rotating an
# entry rotates the exit node, and a lookup with the download after it stays on
# a single address, which is what PrivatBank's session cookie requires.
#
# Verified against a live daemon: four usernames, four distinct exit IPs, and
# the same username twice giving the same one.
HTTPTunnelPort 0.0.0.0:9080 IsolateSOCKSAuth

# A client and never a relay. Without this a misread option is the difference
# between using the network and carrying other people's traffic on our address.
ClientOnly 1

# Persisted in a volume so the guard relays survive a restart. Guards are meant
# to be sticky — picking three fresh entry points on every deploy is the
# behaviour Tor's design specifically avoids.
DataDirectory /var/lib/tor

Log notice stdout

# Deliberately not set: ExitNodes. Pinning Ukrainian exits would look more
# natural to a Ukrainian bank, but there are few of them, and with StrictNodes
# a bad night for those few is an outage for receipts. PrivatBank answered
# normally from ordinary exits when this was measured.
